# UI Shell & Style Consistency

## Single sources of truth

| Concern | Update here |
|---------|-------------|
| Nav routes & labels | `frontend/src/lib/navConfig.ts` |
| Desktop + mobile layout | `frontend/src/components/shell/AppShell*.tsx` |
| Shared rigid styles | `frontend/src/index.css` (`.app-*` classes) |

Never duplicate nav items or shell markup in pages.

## Shell variants

- **Authenticated app**: `AppShell` — header (lg+ nav), `AppShellMobile` (bottom nav + menu btn), drawer
- **Login**: `app-auth-shell` class on the page wrapper

When changing layout or nav behavior, use **one** nav per viewport: top nav (lg+) OR `AppShellMobile` (< lg). The menu (☰) button lives only in `AppShellMobile`, never in the header.

## Nav labels

- Use text labels only (no emoji or icon glyphs in nav)
- Desktop top nav: `item.label`; mobile bottom nav: `item.shortLabel`
- Use `AppNavLink` with variant `desktop` | `mobile`

## Menus & tabs

- Primary page tabs → `AppTabMenu` + `.app-tab-menu` CSS
- Segmented sub-nav → `AppSubnav` + `.app-subnav` CSS
- Mobile: menus scroll horizontally (CSS in `index.css`); do not create one-off mobile tab styles in pages

## Style rules

- Rigid/square UI: use `.surface-card`, `.app-nav-*`, `.app-tab-*` — avoid ad-hoc `rounded-*` or shadows on shells
- YUCG palette only: `--deep-navy`, `--pale-sky`, `--steel-blue`, `--accent`
- New shell UI → add classes to `index.css` under the App shell section, not inline Tailwind in multiple files

## Checklist for nav/feature changes

1. Add route in `App.tsx` and `navConfig.ts`
2. Verify desktop (lg+ top nav only) and mobile/tablet (< lg bottom nav + drawer; no top nav strip)
4. Run `npm run build` in `frontend/`
